  "body": "## Summary\n\nFollow-on design ticket from #5686 — its decomposition sketch names this as a separate design, and the parent's acceptance requires these tickets to be filed and linked. Filed in the 2026-11-04 gap pass (WS-F) so the design work exists and can be prioritised on its own merits; implementation timing is a separate decision, possibly months out.\n\n## What this design must settle\n\nBuffering, backfill, cached grants, and per-class actuation rules when providers go offline or degrade.\n\n## Context from the parent\n\nThe parent design fixes the single capability-provider model — declaration, discovery, negotiation, least-privilege grants — instantiated by ESP32/MQTT, terminal, Bevy, smartphone, and web providers. The parent issue carries the surrounding decisions this ticket must not re-decide; where this ticket's answer would change a parent decision, record that explicitly rather than silently forking it.\n\n## Decision record expected\n\nClose this design with a recorded decision (on this issue or in a `doc/` record linked from it): the chosen shape, the alternatives rejected and why, and the invariants implementation must hold. If the design splits further, file the splits and link them here rather than growing this issue.\n\n## Relations\n\nParent: #5686. Programme: epic #2056. Filed by WS-F (2026-11-04 ID design gap & expansion pass).\n",
